  "report": {
    "rowCount": 221,
    "anomalies": [
      "spine, widget-strawberries-c1: the 4 flagged rows are all one finding — Forsaken City's winged berry count. src-ink-collectables self-describes two winged berries (berry 3, \"this is a flying strawberry\"; berry 19, \"another winged strawberry\") while src-tracker-maps marks one winged berry in chapter 1. Spot-read against both sources: the flags are honest, the doubt is real, and it touches only the berry type — the route text is unaffected. No other chapter conflicts: prose and pack agree exactly at 1/2/1/1/3/0 winged for chapters 2, 3, 4, 5, 7 and Core.",
      "widget-achievements: \"Real Gamer\" (Complete Celeste for PICO-8) and \"1UP!\" (Get a 1UP) are tracked only as checklist rows — no manifested source gives either a location, so the spine emits no step for them. Owning pass: source-gathering. Both are in the 32-achievement completion definition, so the guide is playable but cannot route the player to them.",
      "spine: the C-Sides chapter intro states the unlock rule (\"C-Sides are unlocked after completing 8B, which, in turn, requires completion of all B-Sides\") sourced from celeste.ink's standalone \"Alternate sides\" page, which no sources.json entry covers. Chapter intros carry no sourceRefs so this is not a schema violation, but the provenance is unrecorded. Owning pass: source-gathering — append src-ink-alternate-sides.",
      "data: three defects in layers/data.json were worked around by the spine and widget passes rather than corrected at source, so a re-run of extract-data would still reproduce them. (1) The strawberry-route `type` column is under-populated — ten berries whose own prose calls them winged or flying are typed normal; correcting it dissolves the winged conflicts the data pass recorded for chapters 2, 3, 4, 5 and 7. (2) The chapter-6 checkpoint labels are shifted one section early because Reflection's \"Lake\" checkpoint is omitted, leaving 6_a_5 as the placeholder \"Sub-map 5\". (3) chapters.chapter-6-reflection carries red-strawberries \"3\", which no other source supports and which would make the game total 178 rather than 175. Owning pass: extract-data.",
      "data, widget-pins-core-a-heart-of-the-mountain-section-3: src-tracker-maps carries no crystal-heart pin anywhere in Core, though \"Heart of the Mountain — Collect the Crystal Heart in Chapter 8\" is one of the 32 achievements. The spine and the Sides & Hearts matrix source that heart from src-ink-collectables instead. Not a blocker; recorded against the pack.",
      "widget-strawberries-c*, widget-pins-*: each of the 175 red strawberries is three separate checkables — its route step, its chapter-table row, and its map pin — and only the route step feeds celeste:strawberries' 30/80/175 counters. This is deliberate (Pierre 2026-07-30, approved with the widget stage) and unavoidable for the pins, since mapPinsWidget has no informational-pin option and the berry-to-pin join was tested and rejected in extract-data. Recorded so the guide's checkable total (761) is not mistaken for 761 distinct objectives.",
      "ra-mapping: not applicable. Celeste has no RetroAchievements set, so no ra-mapping layer exists, no step carries achievementRefs, no ra-mapping.json was assembled, and library.json carries no raGameId. The 32 Steam/Xbox/PlayStation achievements are tracked by hand through widget-achievements.",
      "library.json: celeste is still status \"in-compilation\". QA does not change it — flipping it to \"playable\" is what surfaces the guide in the app and is Pierre's call at merge."
    ],
    "flaggedItemIds": [
      "celeste:v-forsaken-city-a-start-1:s3",
      "celeste:v-forsaken-city-a-chasm-1:s5",
